+Device reconstruction uses 00462b30. Active CYWindow roots use 004e01f0;
+CYWidget children instead use virtual +0x114 / 0051a8e0 with LTRB boxes. Their
+geometry members are +0x18/+0x1c/+0x20(height)/+0x24(width); root members differ.
+The status caption has a separate property-42 box and virtual +0x1b8 setter.
+Borrowed old primary/offscreen references in CYWindow+0x38 are rebound before
+painting. AP75/AP92 follow the bottom of the world without reapplying their
+original centered-dialog flags; ordinary front-end dialogs rerun native placement.
+
+View descriptor 0 comes from camera manager 006d84b8 through 00437e40; its
+camera is descriptor+8. Camera virtual +0x54 / 005c2bc0 changes the viewport and
+backing store but leaves clipping-region bounds from construction. The adapter
+also updates those through 005055b0 and 00505520, and the constructor's cached
+width/height at +0x70/+0x74. It gets the world box through the same HUD widget
+2003 virtual +0x28 getter as the original camera constructor. Camera-manager
++8 is rebound to the replacement renderer. Renderer state/view are restored
